# The release machine's identity. On Mac copy to
# artifacts/release-work/release.env in the repository and fill in.
# Windows and Linux use ~/.umbratic/release.env.
# `npm run desktop:release` and the Veil Console
# release script read it; nothing in the repository does. Keep it readable by
# you alone (chmod 600).
#
# Values on the command line win over this file. Quotes around a value are
# allowed and stripped.

# --- Web search: the Brave subscription key baked into a Veil bundle ---------
# Ours, not the customer's: it buys searches on our credit plan, and every
# customer bundle carries the same one. `npm run veil-console:release` bakes it
# into that customer's `veil` binary, so it never reaches the release zip,
# SHA256SUMS, or the customer's server as a file. Leave it empty and the bundle
# simply has no web search, which is a complete product; how many searches a
# customer bought stays a per-release flag (`--searches-per-month`).
# The Veil Console release runs under Linux or WSL, so the file it reads is the
# Linux home's ~/.umbratic/release.env, not the Windows one.
UMBRATIC_BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# --- macOS: notarization ----------------------------------------------------
# Import a Developer ID Application certificate with its private key into your
# keychain, or set CSC_LINK (P12 path/base64) and CSC_KEY_PASSWORD.
# Choose ONE complete notarization credential set.
APPLE_ID=
APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# Alternative App Store Connect API credentials:
# APPLE_API_KEY=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_API_ISSUER=

# --- Windows: Azure Trusted Signing (the Windows machine only) ---------------
# All four are shown on the Trusted Signing account in the Azure portal. The
# publisher is the exact Subject common name of the certificate profile, as
# printed by the account's identity validation — installed apps verify each
# update against it, so it must not change between releases.
# Signing in is `az login` (Azure CLI) once per machine; alternatively export
# AZURE_TENANT_ID, AZURE_CLIENT_ID and AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET for a service
# principal here.
UMBRATIC_WIN_SIGN_ENDPOINT=https://eus.codesigning.azure.net
UMBRATIC_WIN_SIGN_ACCOUNT=
UMBRATIC_WIN_SIGN_PROFILE=
UMBRATIC_WIN_SIGN_PUBLISHER=
